# Quarter-car test rig, HMMWV front corner: sprung mass on a vertical
# prismatic joint, double-wishbone suspension, and a shaker post under the
# wheel acting as the vertical position driver. Hardpoints, masses, and
# inertias are the HMMWV front suspension data shipped with Project Chrono
# (data/vehicle/hmmwv/): suspension HMMWV_DoubleWishboneFront.json, chassis
# 2086.52 kg (quartered), wheel 18.8 kg + tire 37.6 kg, tire radius 0.467.
#
# Axes are ISO vehicle: x forward, y outboard, z up. The base frame sits at
# the DESIGN WHEEL CENTER (Chrono suspension frame minus the wheel-center
# offset (-0.040, 0.910, -0.026)), so every loop closes exactly at q = 0
# with the spindle at identity quaternion, zero position.
#
# Topology (tree DOF 10, nc 8, mobility 2):
#   0 chassis  prismatic z   quarter sprung mass, free heave
#   1 LCA      revolute x    lower wishbone on the chassis; Chrono's pivot
#                            axis is exactly x (front/back pivots at y=0.307)
#   2 UCA      revolute x    upper wishbone; the real pivot axis is skewed
#                            ~13 deg from x (anti-dive), idealized to x here
#                            since tree joints are axis-aligned; pivot placed
#                            at the front/back midpoint
#   3 spindle  floating      upright + spindle + wheel + tire lumped (no
#                            wheel-spin DOF), located by the loop joints
#   4 post     prismatic z   shaker pad at the contact patch: THE POSITION
#                            DRIVER. Drive q[10] through tau[9] (e.g. a stiff
#                            PD servo tracking the road/post profile)
#
# Loop joints (the spindle has ball joints everywhere, so it is a floating
# body pinned by constraints -- spherical tree joints aren't implemented):
#   spherical  LCA outer ball  -> spindle lower ball
#   spherical  UCA outer ball  -> spindle upper ball
#   distance   radius rod, chassis -> spindle steering arm (Chrono's tie-rod
#              hardpoints); kills the leftover spin about the kingpin axis
#   distance   driver rod, post pad -> wheel center, length = tire radius:
#              a rigid "tire" with balls at patch and hub. It pins spindle
#              height to post height; lateral scrub during travel just tilts
#              it (height error is second order, ~s^2/2r)
#
# Mobility 2 = chassis heave + post position. Suspension deflection is their
# difference through the linkage. Tire loads apply via fext on the spindle.
#
# The real HMMWV coil spring and shock (data/vehicle/hmmwv/suspension/
# HMMWV_DoubleWishboneFront.json) are modeled as two separate TSDAs sharing
# the LCA mount point but not the chassis mount point (real geometry: the
# shock is seated further up than the spring). Coordinates converted to this
# file's base/LCA frames the same way every other hardpoint here was (Chrono
# chassis-relative point minus the wheel-center offset (-0.040, 0.910,
# -0.026); the LCA-frame point additionally minus the LCA pivot (0, 0.307,
# 0) in that same Chrono frame):
#   spring: chassis (0.104, 0.510, 0.197) -> base (0.144, -0.400, 0.223)
#           arm     (0.097, 0.543, -0.047) -> LCA (0.097, 0.236, -0.047)
#   shock:  chassis (0.104, 0.498, 0.323) -> base (0.144, -0.412, 0.349)
#           arm     same point as the spring's
# The JSON spring is a nonlinear curve (progressive, free length 0.339 m);
# this format only has a linear TSDA, so k is the curve's slope at zero
# deflection (3629.923 N / 0.02 m). The shock's damping coefficient is
# already linear and used directly. Both are passive (no 'input').
#
# q layout (nq 11, nv 10): q[0] chassis, q[1] LCA, q[2] UCA, q[3..9] spindle
# quaternion + position, q[10] post. Design pose: q = 0 with q[3] = 1.

gravity 0 0 -9.81
stab 0.05

body                     # 0: chassis, quarter sprung mass on vertical slider
parent -1
joint prismatic z
tree 0 0 0
mass 521.6
cg 0 -0.910 0.283        # vehicle centerline, HMMWV CG height (~0.75 above ground)
inertia 88 133 150 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 1: lower control arm, pivot y=0.307 z=0 (Chrono, exact x axis)
parent 0
joint revolute x
tree 0.040 -0.603 0.026
mass 23.965
cg 0 0.240 -0.059
inertia 0.4 0.4 0.8938 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 2: upper control arm, pivot at front/back midpoint
parent 0
joint revolute x
tree -0.118 -0.448 0.2465
mass 5.813
cg 0.052 0.127 -0.0025
inertia 0.03 0.03 0.06276 0 0 0
fext 0

body                     # 3: spindle assembly (upright + spindle + wheel + tire),
parent -1                #    frame at the wheel center
joint floating
tree 0 0 0
mass 90.555
cg 0 -0.0342 0           # upright CG sits 0.159 inboard of the wheel center
inertia 4.896 7.581 4.774 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 4: shaker post pad at the contact patch -- the driver
parent -1
joint prismatic z
tree 0 0 -0.467
mass 25
cg 0 0 0
inertia 0.35 0.35 0.65 0 0 0
fext 0

loop                     # lower ball joint: LCA outer end to spindle
predecessor 1
successor 3
joint spherical
ptree -0.036 0.480 -0.118
stree 0.004 -0.123 -0.092

loop                     # upper ball joint: UCA outer end to spindle
predecessor 2
successor 3
joint spherical
ptree 0.105 0.254 -0.0055
stree -0.013 -0.194 0.241

loop                     # radius rod: chassis to the spindle steering arm
predecessor 0
successor 3
joint distance
ptree -0.210 -0.462 0.080
stree -0.136 -0.089 0.010
length 0.3866588

loop                     # driver rod: post pad to wheel center, one tire radius
predecessor 4
successor 3
joint distance
ptree 0 0 0
stree 0 0 0
length 0.467

poi springChassis 0 0.144 -0.400 0.223
poi springArm 1 0.097 0.236 -0.047
poi shockChassis 0 0.144 -0.412 0.349
poi shockArm 1 0.097 0.236 -0.047

tsda spring                # HMMWV front coil spring, linearized (see header)
from springChassis
to springArm
k 181496.15
c 0
l0 0.339

tsda shock                 # HMMWV front shock absorber
from shockChassis
to shockArm
k 0
c 19015.5692
l0 0.339
